---
// cookie-policy.astro
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Cookie Policy – Toolivo"
  description="Understand how Toolivo uses non-intrusive cookies and browser local storage to maintain session state and display compliant advertising."
  canonicalPath="/cookie-policy/"
>
  <div class="container" style="padding-top: 2.5rem; padding-bottom: 5rem;">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'Cookie Policy' }]} />

    <article style="max-width: 820px; margin: 2rem auto;">
      <header style="margin-bottom: 3rem;">
        <span class="badge badge-primary" style="margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">Compliance</span>
        <h1 style="margin-bottom: 1rem;">Cookie Policy</h1>
        <p style="color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.95rem;">Last updated: October 1, 2026</p>
      </header>

      <div class="blog-content" style="font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--text-secondary);">
        <h2>1. What Are Cookies?</h2>
        <p>
          Cookies are small text fragments placed on your device to retain user preferences (such as dark/light mode) and support essential website functionality.
        </p>

        <h2>2. How Toolivo Uses Cookies & Local Storage</h2>
        <p>
          Toolivo minimizes cookie usage to the strictest standard:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Essential Storage:</strong> We use your browser's native <code>localStorage</code> to store your tool preferences (e.g. compression quality settings) and anonymized local usage metrics. This data never leaves your device.</li>
          <li><strong>Advertising Partners:</strong> Our third-party advertising partners (such as Google AdSense) may set cookies to deliver contextual, non-intrusive advertisements and prevent ad fraud.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>3. Managing Your Cookie Preferences</h2>
        <p>
          You can restrict or block cookies at any time through your browser settings. Blocking cookies will not prevent you from using any of our free tools.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
